Now let me make sure about the characterization once more. We require for every position $i$ in subarray: $(S - a_i) \% k == 0$. This means all $a_i$ are congruent mod $k$ (since $S - a_i \equiv 0$ and $S - a_j \equiv 0$ gives $a_i \equiv a_j$). And $a_i \equiv S$. Let common residue be $r$. Then $S \equiv mr$, so $r \equiv mr$, i.e., $(m-1)r \equiv 0$. Conversely if all $a_i \equiv r$ and $(m-1)r \equiv 0$, then $S \equiv mr \equiv r$, so $S - a_i \equiv r - r = 0$. Correct.

